# The FFmpeg the macOS app ships (scripts/package/macos-app.sh): jellyfin-ffmpeg's
# portable macOS builds, GPL, with every library linked in statically, one
# per architecture, made into one universal ffmpeg and one ffprobe. It is
# the FFmpeg the Docker image has (the Dockerfile's JELLYFIN_FFMPEG_VERSION),
# so the app plays what the image plays, Dolby Vision with tonemapx included.
# Each release attaches its complete source
# (scripts/package/ffmpeg-macos-source.sh).
#
# To move to a newer one: the release's portable_macarm64-gpl and
# portable_mac64-gpl assets with their SHA-256 (the release page lists
# each asset's), and the commit its tag points at.
JELLYFIN_FFMPEG_VERSION=8.1.3-1
JELLYFIN_FFMPEG_COMMIT=253db2a7b0a8045c54ce68ce33d7f601229b1822
ARM64_ASSET=jellyfin-ffmpeg_8.1.3-1_portable_macarm64-gpl.tar.xz
ARM64_SHA256=22445d7299742749ad2eeb9ce87963d50def0357e45b3e6c7b69987c8365dbf6
X86_64_ASSET=jellyfin-ffmpeg_8.1.3-1_portable_mac64-gpl.tar.xz
X86_64_SHA256=cb2b5c154d49a6b6bfe29fa6c16510e85dcbf60b805764121a167b093d4bb6fb
